#: ../../site/index.rst:1
msgid ""
"Impact of Export Controls on the Future of Open Source AI: an illustrated "
"literary and evidentiary book on how software, model-weight, and silicon "
"hardware borders reshape human progress."
msgstr ""
"수출 통제가 오픈소스 AI의 미래에 미치는 영향: 소프트웨어, 모델 가중치, 실리콘 하드웨어의 국경 장벽이 인류의 진보를 어떻게 "
"재편하는지 1차 사료와 게임이론으로 밝혀낸 일러스트 논픽션."

#: ../../site/index.rst:5
msgid "Impact of Export Controls on the Future of Open Source AI"
msgstr "수출 통제가 오픈소스 AI의 미래에 미치는 영향"

#: ../../site/index.rst:10
msgid ""
"AN ILLUSTRATED BOOK ON OPEN MINDS, SILICON HARDWARE, AND HUMAN PROGRESS"
msgstr "열린 지성, 실리콘 하드웨어, 그리고 인류의 진보에 관한 일러스트 도서"

#: ../../site/index.rst:14
msgid ""
"*\"He who lights his taper at mine, receives light without darkening me.\"* "
"Jefferson's 1813 image captures the promise of knowledge that can be shared "
"without being used up. This book asks how controls on models and computing "
"hardware can interrupt that exchange. `JEFFERSON "
"<https://founders.archives.gov/documents/Jefferson/03-06-02-0322>`_"
msgstr ""
" *내 불로 촛불을 켜는 이는 나를 어둡게 하지 않고 빛을 얻는다.*  1813년 비유에서 출발해 모델·장비 통제가 지식 교환에 미치는 "
"영향을 묻습니다. `JEFFERSON "
"<https://founders.archives.gov/documents/Jefferson/03-06-02-0322>`_"

#: ../../site/index.rst:18
msgid ""
"`Begin Reading the Book <read-cover_>`_ `Download Typeset PDF Book <book-"
"pdf_>`_ `Explore All 40 Checkpoints <read-atlas_>`_ `Official Approval & "
"Contacts <read-contacts_>`_"
msgstr ""
"`책 읽기 시작하기 <read-cover_>`_ `조판 PDF 도서 다운로드 <book-pdf_>`_ `40개 통제 지점 모두 보기 "
"<read-atlas_>`_ `공식 허가 절차 및 연락처 <read-contacts_>`_"

#: ../../site/index.rst:23 ../../site/index.rst:28
msgid ""
"A border barrier holds up computer parts and technical plans while two "
"research teams try to work together."
msgstr "두 연구팀이 협력하려 하지만 국경 장벽이 컴퓨터 부품과 기술 도면의 이동을 막습니다."

#: ../../site/index.rst:30
msgid "From an Open Republic of Ideas to a Guarded Horizon"
msgstr "열린 사상의 공화국에서 검문소가 세워진 지평선으로"

#: ../../site/index.rst:33
msgid ""
"An open model can let a university, a small business or a language project "
"adapt a shared tool. These possibilities do not guarantee safety or equal "
"access. Our argument is that broad restrictions can damage cooperation even "
"when each country hopes to gain an advantage."
msgstr ""
"공개 모델은 대학·작은 기업·언어 프로젝트를 돕지만 안전·평등을 보장하지 않습니다. 각자 우위를 추구해도 넓은 제한은 협력을 해칠 수 "
"있습니다."

#: ../../site/index.rst:35
msgid ""
"Open AI also needs physical computers. Large training runs can require "
"advanced chips, memory and networks; smaller models can run on more ordinary"
" equipment. Controls on hardware and design knowledge can affect access even"
" when a model has a permissive license."
msgstr "공개 AI는 컴퓨터가 필요합니다. 큰 학습과 작은 모델의 장비는 다르며 개방 라이선스도 장비 접근 문제를 없애지는 않습니다."

#: ../../site/index.rst:39 ../../site/index.rst:44
msgid ""
"Open models depend on chips, memory and computing infrastructure. A "
"restriction on one part can affect access to the whole system."
msgstr "공개 모델은 칩·메모리·계산 기반에 의존합니다. 일부 제한은 전체 접근에 영향을 줄 수 있습니다."

#: ../../site/index.rst:48
msgid ""
"**Hardware:** US rules cover specified chips and manufacturing items. China "
"proposes controls on specified processor and memory designs and certain "
"technologies for clusters with more than 10,000 cards. The scope depends on "
"the precise item and conditions. `CN-A1 "
"<https://insanai.github.io/aiexportcontrols/sources/announcement-48-attachment-1.pdf>`_"
" `US26 "
"<https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-2026-01-15/html/2026-00789.htm>`_ "
"`EAR734 <https://www.bis.gov/regulations/ear/734>`_"
msgstr ""
" **장비:**  미국은 지정 물품, 중국 제안은 특정 설계·1만 장 초과 기술입니다. 범위는 실제 대상·조건에 달렸습니다. `CN-A1"
" "
"<https://insanai.github.io/aiexportcontrols/sources/announcement-48-attachment-1.pdf>`_"
" `US26 "
"<https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-2026-01-15/html/2026-00789.htm>`_ "
"`EAR734 <https://www.bis.gov/regulations/ear/734>`_"

#: ../../site/index.rst:49
msgid ""
"**Models:** Chinese temporary registration has started, while new catalogue "
"prohibitions and restrictions remain proposed. US model-weight text and its "
"announced non-enforcement policy are separate questions. `CN48 "
"<https://www.mofcom.gov.cn/zwgk/zcfb/art/2026/art_0a31a3c9ac404f7a9b0e917ce3412997.html>`_"
" `CN-A1 "
"<https://insanai.github.io/aiexportcontrols/sources/announcement-48-attachment-1.pdf>`_"
" `EAR774 <https://www.bis.gov/regulations/ear/774>`_ `GAO26 "
"<https://www.gao.gov/products/b-337935>`_"
msgstr ""
" **모델:**  등록은 시작됐고 새 분류는 제안입니다. 미국 문구와 불집행을 구분합니다. `CN48 "
"<https://www.mofcom.gov.cn/zwgk/zcfb/art/2026/art_0a31a3c9ac404f7a9b0e917ce3412997.html>`_"
" `CN-A1 "
"<https://insanai.github.io/aiexportcontrols/sources/announcement-48-attachment-1.pdf>`_"
" `EAR774 <https://www.bis.gov/regulations/ear/774>`_ `GAO26 "
"<https://www.gao.gov/products/b-337935>`_"

#: ../../site/index.rst:51
msgid "The Fortress Trap: How Both Sides Can Lose"
msgstr "요새의 함정: 양쪽이 함께 잃는 구조"

#: ../../site/index.rst:54
msgid ""
"Two countries can each choose a broad wall because they fear giving the "
"other an advantage. In the book's illustrative game, both then receive 5, "
"although both would prefer the 17 available through mutual sharing. This is "
"a possible cooperation failure, not proof that every export control harms "
"every participant. `GAME <https://www.cs.cornell.edu/~rafael/networks-"
"html/chapter1.html>`_"
msgstr ""
"상대 우위를 걱정해 모두 장벽을 택하면 예에서는 각5, 협력하면17입니다. 가능한 협력 실패이지 모든 통제의 피해 증명이 아닙니다. "
"`GAME <https://www.cs.cornell.edu/~rafael/networks-html/chapter1.html>`_"

#: ../../site/index.rst:56 ../../site/index.rst:61
msgid ""
"Two teams finish a computer by sharing parts and knowledge, then struggle "
"when a wall separates them. This illustrates the assumed game, not a "
"measured outcome."
msgstr ""
"두 팀이 부품과 지식을 공유하면 컴퓨터를 완성하지만 벽으로 나뉘면 어려워집니다. 가정한 게임의 예시이며 실측 결과가 아닙니다."

#: ../../site/index.rst:65
msgid "Assumed scores in the teaching game"
msgstr "설명용 게임의 가정한 점수"

#: ../../site/index.rst:65
msgid ""
"#import \"figures/diagrams.typ\": game-theory-matrix\n"
"#game-theory-matrix(lang: \"en\")"
msgstr ""
"#import \"figures/diagrams.typ\": game-theory-matrix\n"
"#game-theory-matrix(lang: \"ko\")"

#: ../../site/index.rst:72
msgid ""
"The book explains why the result follows from its assumptions, what could "
"reverse it, and how a repeated relationship can make cooperation worthwhile."
" It also separates the possible benefits of public auditing from the risks "
"of wider access. Our case for precise controls and workable open-research "
"routes does not depend on invented loss estimates. `NTIA "
"<https://www.ntia.gov/sites/default/files/publications/ntia-ai-open-model-"
"report.pdf>`_ `OPENRISK <https://arxiv.org/abs/2403.07918>`_"
msgstr ""
"가정·반례·반복 협력을 설명하고 감사 이익과 접근 위험을 구분합니다. 주장은 가상 손실 수치에 의존하지 않습니다. `NTIA "
"<https://www.ntia.gov/sites/default/files/publications/ntia-ai-open-model-"
"report.pdf>`_ `OPENRISK <https://arxiv.org/abs/2403.07918>`_"

#: ../../site/index.rst:74
msgid ""
"The legal records and research references distinguish what is already "
"operating, what remains proposed, and what is our analysis. They support "
"three practical reading habits:"
msgstr "출처는 현재 조치·제안·분석을 나누고 세 읽기 습관을 제시합니다."

#: ../../site/index.rst:76
msgid ""
"**Distinguish public files from first releases.** Existing public "
"technology, private derivatives and new open-source exports can take "
"different routes. A copyright license is not a government permit. `CN-A1 "
"<https://insanai.github.io/aiexportcontrols/sources/announcement-48-attachment-1.pdf>`_"
" `EAR774 <https://www.bis.gov/regulations/ear/774>`_"
msgstr ""
" **기존 공개와 첫 공개를 구별합니다.**  파생판·신규 수출은 경로가 다르며 저작권은 정부 승인이 아닙니다. `CN-A1 "
"<https://insanai.github.io/aiexportcontrols/sources/announcement-48-attachment-1.pdf>`_"
" `EAR774 <https://www.bis.gov/regulations/ear/774>`_"

#: ../../site/index.rst:77
msgid ""
"**Keep current registration separate from the draft.** China has begun "
"temporary registration for covered transfers; new prohibitions and "
"facilitated licensing remain proposals. `CN48 "
"<https://www.mofcom.gov.cn/zwgk/zcfb/art/2026/art_0a31a3c9ac404f7a9b0e917ce3412997.html>`_"
" `CNQA "
"<https://www.mofcom.gov.cn/zwgk/zcjd/art/2026/art_b11d5c1e9374421e93e85dc87eba6e38.html>`_"
msgstr ""
" **등록과 초안을 구별합니다.**  등록은 시행 중, 새 금지·편의는 제안입니다. `CN48 "
"<https://www.mofcom.gov.cn/zwgk/zcfb/art/2026/art_0a31a3c9ac404f7a9b0e917ce3412997.html>`_"
" `CNQA "
"<https://www.mofcom.gov.cn/zwgk/zcjd/art/2026/art_b11d5c1e9374421e93e85dc87eba6e38.html>`_"

#: ../../site/index.rst:78
msgid ""
"**Read deadlines in their proper scope.** The standard licensing clocks do "
"not promise the total duration of a project or the future automatic-"
"licensing process. The book links the responsible authorities and their "
"source records. `CNTIER "
"<https://xzfg.moj.gov.cn/front/law/detail?LawID=898>`_ `CNMEAS "
"<https://www.mofcom.gov.cn/dl/file/20211203230621.pdf>`_"
msgstr ""
" **범위 안에서 기간을 읽습니다.**  프로젝트 총기간이나 미래 절차를 보장하지 않으며 기관·원전을 연결합니다. `CNTIER "
"<https://xzfg.moj.gov.cn/front/law/detail?LawID=898>`_ `CNMEAS "
"<https://www.mofcom.gov.cn/dl/file/20211203230621.pdf>`_"

